    "updated_at": "2025-09-04T04:37:23Z",
    "body": "#11620 says\n\n> adds a default crossorigin mode of \"cors\" anonymous (necessary for dictionaries to be usable in a third-party context).\n\nbut I don't think that's necessarily a reason to remove the usual requirement that if a resource is to be usable in third-party contexts, web developers explicitly add a `crossorigin=\"\"` attribute.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
