    "created_at": "2025-09-04T15:48:03Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-09-04T15:48:03Z",
    "body": "Compression dictionaries MUST be CORS-readable to be stored and used for future requests (because they can be used for oracle attacks, they can only be used where the content is directly readable already).\n\nBecause of that, no-cors is not a useful default for compression dictionaries and the concern is that developers will add the link tags but forget to explicitly set an appropriate crossorigin policy (we have history with this being a problem with preconnect and preload for fonts which have similar CORS issues). Same-site dictionaries would work fine but any cross-origin dictionaries would be fetched but silently dropped.\n\nAnonymous is the most sensible default CORS mode for a stand-alone compression dictionary since they are geared towards common patterns across a site without user-specific data (and if sites aren't careful, including private user data in them can lead to issues).",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/whatwg/html/issues/comments/3254362670/reactions",
